.TH RASPIBACKUPCONFIG 1 "@DATE@" "raspiBackup @VERSION@" "raspiBackup Manual"
.SH NAME
raspiBackupConfig \- install and configure raspiBackup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raspiBackupConfig
.br
.B raspiBackupConfig
.BR \-i " | " \-u " | " \-U
.RB [ \-t
.BR crond | systemd ]
.br
.B raspiBackupConfig
.BR \-h | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raspiBackupConfig
is a menu driven tool to configure the most important options of
.BR raspiBackup (1)
and to set up regular backups.
It writes the configuration file
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
(see
.BR raspiBackup.conf (5)).
.PP
Called without options it starts an interactive
.BR whiptail (1)
user interface with the following main menu entries:
.TP
.B M1 Language
Select the language of the user interface and of
.BR raspiBackup .
.TP
.B M2 Install raspiBackup
Add the signed
.B raspiBackup
apt repository and install the Debian package
.B raspibackup
with
.BR apt-get (8)
using a default configuration.
.TP
.B M3 Configure major options
Configure backup path, backup type, backup mode, number of backups to keep
or smart recycle, services to stop and start, partitions to back up,
compression, message detail, eMail notification, clone device and the
regular backup (enable or disable it, weekday and time).
.TP
.B M4 Uninstall raspiBackup
Uninstall
.B raspiBackup
with
.BR apt-get (8)
and remove the apt repository.
.TP
.B M5 Update components
Update
.B raspiBackup
or the installer.
.TP
.B M9 About and useful links
Version information and links to the documentation.
.PP
Regular backups are run either by a
.BR systemd (1)
timer or by
.BR cron (8).
systemd is used if it is available, unless a cron configuration already
exists or
.B \-t
is given.
.PP
.B raspiBackupConfig
has to be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display a short help text and exit.
.TP
.B \-i
Unattended install of
.B raspiBackup
with
.BR apt-get (8).
.TP
.BR \-t " crond" | systemd
Use cron or systemd for regular backups.
.TP
.B \-u
Unattended uninstall of
.B raspiBackup
with
.BR apt-get (8).
.TP
.B \-U
Unattended update of
.BR raspiBackupConfig .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the version and exit.
.SH NOTES
If
.B raspiBackup
is installed as Debian package
.BR raspibackup ,
the options
.B \-i
and
.B \-U
are not available.
Use
.BR apt (8)
to update the package instead:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade
.fi
.RE
.PP
When the package is removed, the systemd units and the cron file created
by
.B raspiBackupConfig
are removed as well.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
Configuration of
.BR raspiBackup .
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/raspibackup/raspiBackup_{en,de}.conf
Configuration templates.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/raspiBackup.{service,timer}
systemd units for regular backups.
For other intervals than daily or weekly edit the timer manually.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/raspiBackup
cron file for regular backups.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/raspibackup.sources
.br
.I /usr/share/keyrings/raspibackup-archive-keyring.gpg
apt repository of
.B raspiBackup
and its signing key.
.TP
.I ./raspiBackupConfig.log
Log file, written into the current directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR raspiBackup (1),
.BR raspiBackup.conf (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR crontab (5)
.PP
Full documentation:
.UR https://raspibackup.linux-tips-and-tricks.de/en/home/
.UE
